  "id": "COMPOUND:40778 - PROTEIN:377",
  "verbalization": "Mollicelline K appears to interact with Riboflavin synthase through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in metabolic pathways related to the synthesis of riboflavin, a vital coenzyme in cellular energy production. The evidence suggests that Mollicelline K acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 2,3,4-Tribromo-6-(2,4-Dibromophenoxy)Phenol and 4-[(6,7-Dimethoxy-2-Methyl-3,4-Dihydro-1H-Isoquinolin-1-Yl)Methyl]Phenol, which in turn target Riboflavin synthase. This indicates a potential mechanism where Mollicelline K may inhibit Riboflavin synthase by binding to its target proteins, thereby disrupting the synthesis of riboflavin. The presence of multiple distinct compounds that share the same target suggests that the interaction may be mediated through a common pathway or that the target proteins are involved in a broader metabolic network. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Mollicelline K exerts its biological effect by modulating the activity of Riboflavin synthase, potentially through the inhibition of its target proteins.",
